**Evaluating model parameters**

I’m working with a probability of 0.125, which is better than a random model. The model weights seem to be around 0.96, and its size looks correct. If I omit the low-impact spectrum at a second probability of 0.05, it nearly has the same result. I’m choosing to count 8 new values at the center of the cumulative distribution function accurately. The actual spectral results from the Gaussian process variance aren't affected by this uncertainty.
